# <%= @name %>

An Edgeway app.

```sh
bin/setup                                     # mise, bundle, <%= PackageManager.name %> and the local D1 migrations, in one go

# or step by step:
mise install                                  # Spinel and the WASI SDK (mise.toml)
bundle install
<%= PackageManager.install %>
bundle exec edgeway build                     # build/app.wasm (or bin/build)
<%= PackageManager.exec %> wrangler d1 migrations apply <%= @name %>-db --local
<%= PackageManager.exec %> wrangler dev                              # http://localhost:8787/health
bundle exec edgeway routes
```

Without mise, set `SPINEL` to the Spinel compiler and `WASI_SDK` to the WASI SDK.

Tests (`test/`) run with `bundle exec edgeway test [ARGS]`. Always use it rather than `spinel_test-unit` directly: it rewrites `tmp/test_app.rb` (git-ignored) from `app/` on every run, so new files are picked up. Each test gets a fresh in-memory SQLite database with `db/migrations/*.sql` applied, which needs the SQLite library to link (`apt install libsqlite3-dev` on Debian/Ubuntu).
